---
description: Colocate UI components with their CVA variants under src/components/ui
globs: src/components/ui/**/*
alwaysApply: true
---

# UI component folders

- Put each shared UI primitive in its own folder under `src/components/ui/`:
  `ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx`, `ComponentName/componentVariants.ts` (or
  `*Variants.ts`), optional siblings (`ButtonLink.tsx`), and `index.ts` that
  re-exports the public API.
- Import from the folder barrel (`@/components/ui/Button`,
  `@/components/ui/Banner`), not from deep file paths or leftover flat files.
- Keep CVA / variant helpers in the same folder as the component. Do not leave
  `buttonVariants.ts` (or similar) as a sibling of many unrelated components.
- Variant modules must stay free of `"use client"` so Server Components can
  call them (e.g. `ButtonLink`). Mark only interactive entry files with
  `"use client"` when they need hooks or browser APIs.
- Style with explicit design tokens (`var(--color-text)`,
  `var(--color-accent)`, …). Avoid short Tailwind theme aliases that alias
  back into the same `--color-*` name (circular). Buttons use the `sl-btn`
  class so legacy global `button { … }` rules do not override contrast.
- Reuse a component that already exists. The project header is
  `LandingHeader` / `ProjectPageHeader`. Nested pages change `title` and add
  breadcrumbs. Do not invent a second header.
